1. Definitions

   "Pluto" means the code in this repository that is released under the
   License, and any version of it that the copyright holder releases.

   "Public Interface" means the parts of Pluto that are meant for other
   code to use:
     a. Apex types and members that Pluto declares as global;
     b. invocable actions and platform events that Pluto ships;
     c. custom objects, custom fields, and custom metadata types that
        Pluto ships, used through standard Salesforce features; and
     d. the rules in the extension contract (force-app/contracts/
        EXTENSIONS.md).

   An "Extension" is a work that uses Pluto only through the Public
   Interface, and that does not contain Pluto code or a changed copy of
   any Pluto file. Examples are a class that implements ITool,
   IModelProvider, IContextProvider, or IToolAuthorizationPolicy; a Flow
   or trigger that calls a Pluto invocable action; and Apex that calls a
   global Pluto method.

